# Sync-tool duplicates. A file-syncing tool watching the working directory produces
# `name 2.ext` when a file is rewritten faster than the tool settles. Four of these were
# committed before anyone noticed. Ignored here and failed by lint:duplicates, because
# ignoring them alone would leave them lying around to be opened by mistake.
* [0-9].*
* [0-9]
*copy.*
*copy [0-9].*

# The generated site. Built by `pnpm site:build` from calibration/table.json, so committing
# it would mean two sources of truth for the same numbers.
apps/site/dist/

# Screenshots. `pnpm screenshots` writes 17 full-page captures at three widths in both colour
# schemes, which is 24 MB and regenerable. Five are committed as the record of what the layout
# looks like, plus audit.json, which is the actual evidence the dogfood gate passed.
docs/screenshots/*.png
!docs/screenshots/home-iphone.png
!docs/screenshots/home-ipad.png
!docs/screenshots/home-desktop.png
!docs/screenshots/accuracy-desktop.png
!docs/screenshots/home-skip-link-focused.png
